  <title>Credit memo</title>

  <p>A credit memo gives a customer credit for products they bought and
  returned. Open it with <guiseq><gui>Customer</gui><gui>Credit
  memo</gui></guiseq>. Like an invoice, it is saved as you type, and a
  customer's unposted credit memo is opened again when you choose them.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Customer</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New item</gui>. In <gui>Product</gui>, choose what
    was returned. The list holds every line of the customer's posted invoices,
    with the invoice number and date beside each, so the credit is at the price
    they paid and the tax they were charged.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Qty</gui> returned, and change the <gui>Price</gui>
    or <gui>Tax</gui> if the credit should differ.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click in <gui>Date returned</gui> to choose the day it came
    back.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the <gui>Date</gui> of the memo and click <gui>Post Credit
    Memo</gui>. The print dialog opens; print to post.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Posting puts the returned products that are counted in inventory back
  into stock, at the location they were sold from and the cost they left at,
  and posts the credit to the customer's account. The credit then counts
  toward their next payment. As with an invoice, check <gui>Cancel printing
  and posting</gui> in the print dialog to stop without posting.</p>

  <p>The window menu has <gui>Delete item</gui>, for the selected line, and
  <gui>View Credit Memo</gui>, to see it before posting.</p>

</page>
